  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Wemos - Innovation and Expertise Hub</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">All 11 members of the Dutch SRHR Alliance contribute significant value to the partnership through governance, programme implementation, learning, and knowledge exchange. Key organizations including Amref, Oxfam Novib, and Wemos provide central management roles, while Hivos, Rutgers, Liliane Fonds, Amref, and Plan International support country-level coordination and mentorship. Choice plays a leading role in strengthening Meaningful and Inclusive Youth Participation across the Alliance&#x2019;s governance structures.

In addition, organizations such as CoC, VSO, and Aidsfonds contribute technical expertise through participation in knowledge exchange meetings,learning sessions, and collaborative activities coordinated by the Alliance Hub. The partnership emphasizes shared learning, innovation, and cross-country collaboration to strengthenprogramme effectiveness and long-term sustainability.
At the global level, the Alliance operates through a Memorandum of Understanding (MoU), while governance modalities will be further refined during the inception phase. Currently, the Directors&#x2019; Meeting&#x2014;comprising representatives from all 11 organizations&#x2014;serves as the principal decision-making body for global planning andbudgeting. Decisions are made through consensus whenever possible, or by a two-thirds majority vote when required.</narrative>
  </description>
